  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Trafficking in Persons (TIP) to Northern Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project, TRAFCORD will bring together a local network of government and non-government agencies to address the migration and humanitarian crisis in Thailands northern borders with Burma and Laos, both Tier 3 countries. TRAFCORD will work to prevent trafficking among individuals migrating to Thailand in search of greater opportunity, with special attention to marginalized populations (e.g., stateless individuals, refugees, and ethnic minorities), especially women and children. This will be accomplished through cross-border interventions, including awareness campaigns targeting migrant workers throughout the migration cycle, and by strengthening the capacity of Thai multidisciplinary teams to work with their cross-border counterparts in Burma and Laos to identify and protect victims. Community centers will be set up in high risk areas and workshops will be held with school-age children, youth leaders, migrant workers, and other high-risk groups to raise awareness of the dangers of exploitation and trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
